## snag-2 (v1) → snag-3 (v2) — 2026-04-28 13:05
Decision: Split into 3 paragraphs (mt-6 / mt-4 / mt-4) instead of 2 or sentence-line breaks.
Alternatives considered: keep one paragraph with a `<br/>` separator; split into 2 paragraphs.
Reason: David's feedback "seems like quite a block" suggested the wall of text was the problem. Three paragraphs map to three discrete ideas (capabilities / score / trust line). Two would still feel dense; line-break-only doesn't visually delimit ideas.
Risk: vertical height of the hero column grew — if it pushes the device mock below the fold on smaller laptops, may need to compress. Captured staging shots show it still fits at 1440x900.

## snag-4 — 2026-04-28 13:10
Decision: Moved 7-card 3+3+1-wide layout to 9-card 3+3+3 (no wide card).
Alternatives considered: 3+3+1+2 (keep wide team-lead card, add 2 new in row 4); 3+3+3+0 (drop team-lead).
Reason: a row of 2 in a 3-column grid is visually awkward. Keeping team-lead as wide and demoting it to standard width preserves the journey but makes all 9 cards parallel. The new cards (Proof, Keeping up) are arguably more important than team-lead since they map directly to the Dynamic Score USP and the Stay Current pricing tier.
Risk: Team lead card was deliberately wide for For Teams sales emphasis. Shrinking it to standard width may dilute that pitch — but the For Teams chevron + clickable card preserves the link.

